{# One kubernetes join token per natively-joining runner, so a `bot_joined` check names
   exactly which runner reached the cluster. `type: oidc` makes teleport fetch the
   issuer's discovery + JWKS at join time from the shared oidc-server, which serves the
   system-trusted wildcard cert (same shape as modules/kubernetes).

   The join METHOD is incidental to what this module tests: the customer uses env0, and
   any method fails identically because the provider's failure happens after the join
   returns. kubernetes is simply the method that needs no cloud provider here. #}
{% for j in native_joiners %}
{% if not loop.first %}---
{% endif %}
kind: token
version: v2
metadata:
  name: {{ j.token }}
spec:
  roles: [Bot]
  bot_name: {{ j.bot }}
  join_method: kubernetes
  kubernetes:
    type: oidc
    oidc:
      issuer: https://oidc.{{ lab_domain }}:8443
    allow:
      - service_account: "default:{{ j.sa }}"
{% endfor %}
